I claim I have a magic penny, a brilliant penny, whose toss can
predict the outcome of the stock market, up or down, for the next n
days. I prepare 2^n envelopes with the penny's "predictions." After
the n days have passed, I simply retrieve the envelope whose sequence
matches the market....then I offer to sell this brilliant penny to
some gullible investor.

All postdictive schemes may involve such errors or scams.

