Tim's exposition on the "brilliant penny" missed a classic con.

Players:

2^N possible con victims
N days

Call the victims and tell them each day your prediction of which way a
stock with equiprobable likelyhood of rising or falling will move.
Tell half one story, half the other. At the end of N days, you will
have convinced one investor that you really really  can predict the
market.

